// Simulate's exact stock on a 3-axis run: brep-bench's cnc/bull-nose-profile
// (`fixtures/cnc/bull-nose-profile.cadrs`): a bull-nose mill (⌀8, corner 1.5) profiles a groove
// round a six-lobed flower in three step-downs, its tip on the flower's arcs. The stock is cut
// as a solid of the kernel's by the tool swept along each arc: its walls cylinders, its
// corners tori, drawn from their own surfaces (no facets, no lattice).
// 01 A fifth of the way: the first lap at −4 part way round, the cut ending in the tool's
//    shape where the tool is.
// 02 Half way: the first lap done, the second (−8) on its way.
// 03 Four fifths: the last lap (−10) going round.
// 04 The end: the groove, its floor's edges rounded by the mill's corner (the case's solid).
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        SetTimeout(240),
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Key("F12"),
        Key("F12"),
        Custom("fixture cnc/bull-nose-profile"),
        Wait(5),
        Click(ui("tab-cam")),
        WaitFor("cam-tree"),
        Wait(5),
        Click(ui("cam-tb-regenerate")),
        Wait(10),
        Click(ui("cam-tb-preview")),
        WaitFor("cam-preview-bar"),
        Click(ui("cam-pv-simulate")),
        Click(ui("cam-pv-part")),
        Custom("cam fit"),
        Wait(5),
        Custom("cam preview-at 0.2"),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(5),
        Screenshot("01-first-lap"),
        Custom("cam preview-at 0.5"),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(5),
        Screenshot("02-second-lap"),
        Custom("cam preview-at 0.8"),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(5),
        Screenshot("03-last-lap"),
        Custom("cam preview-end"),
        MoveTo(1420, 900),
        Wait(10),
        Screenshot("04-end"),
    ],
)
